1.4.0 (2026-09-17)
https://github.com/CodyTolene/pip-boy-3000-holotapes/pull/112
- Added APPINFO-backed MISC artwork using the supplied PIP-CO Startup Systems IMG.
- Added readable source files alongside compact installed runtime files for the UI, startup runtime, and deferred wake loader.
- Removed public diagnostic logging and kept the installed runtime focused on low-memory operation.
- Removed whole-module `ram` directives and tightened temporary source/factory cleanup around deferred runtime loading.
- Fixed post-boot last-frame retention by always stopping owned AVI/audio playback, resetting the display state, and restoring the proven 160 ms Pip-OS handoff delay.
- Preserved the split wake/runtime architecture, optional startup AVI support, Custom Bootups, reset-safe Default Bootup behavior, and stock fallback.

1.3.0 (2026-09-13)
https://github.com/CodyTolene/pip-boy-3000-holotapes/pull/105
- Public release with low-RAM persistent startup runtime, deferred wake loader, reset-safe Default Bootup policy, category scrolling, and optional startup AVI support.

1.2.0 (2026-08-26)
https://github.com/CodyTolene/pip-boy-3000-holotapes/pull/97
- Added automatic detection of up to five user-supplied Custom_Bootup AVI files directly in HOLO/STARTUP_ANIMATIONS/.
- Custom Bootups submenu appears only when at least one supported custom AVI exists.
- No custom folder, JSON descriptor, or core JavaScript editing required.
- Custom scanning occurs only when opening the holotape UI; persistent boot runtime stores/uses only the selected startup index.
- Existing built-in startup behavior and low-memory runtime separation preserved.

1.1.0 (2026-08-21)
https://github.com/CodyTolene/pip-boy-3000-holotapes/pull/83
- Added low-memory runtime separation so the persistent startup hook does not retain the full holotape UI closure.
- Fixed repeated boot-cycle crashes reported as CALLBACK, LOW_MEMORY, and MEMORY on Pip-Boy OS 1.1.6.
- Moved hard-failsafe timing to begin after video playback starts.
- Added the NPC submenu scroll indicator.
- Added Dogmeat and Mr. House startup variants to the modular startup list.
- Kept startup audio embedded in AVI files; no separate WAV dependencies.
- Kept the targeted clean ENCLAVE_PIPBOY.AVI media fix for the 1.1.6 black-video/audio-only case.
- Removed diagnostic PIP-CO logging and runtime APPINFO self-registration from the public modular build.

1.0.0 (2026-08-08)
https://github.com/CodyTolene/pip-boy-3000-holotapes/pull/79
- Initial PIP-CO Startup Systems release.
